# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party COURSEWARE-DERIVED research material — NEVER COMMIT.
#
# THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. The files below are exhaustive, structure-following
# distillations of COMMERCIAL TRAINING COURSES. Individual facts are
# uncopyrightable, but an inventory that tracks a course's own selection and
# arrangement is a derivative of the part copyright actually protects — and the
# source material is marked "not for publication".
#
# THE RULE IS BY CLASS, NOT BY VENDOR. Any paid course, courseware deck,
# workbook, or exam-prep material — SANS/GIAC, 13cubed, Magnet, Cellebrite,
# OffSec, or anything acquired next year — is ignored here the moment it is
# distilled. Add the path when the material lands; do not wait for review.
#
# CITING a vendor's freely published research (a blog post, a conference talk,
# a YouTube video, a tool's own docs) is NOT this. That is ordinary sourcing and
# is encouraged. The line is PAID COURSE CONTENT vs PUBLIC RESEARCH OUTPUT.
#
# The publishable artifact is the DESCRIPTOR: a fact re-verified against an
# independent primary source (Microsoft Learn, MS-* specs, libyal, MITRE ATT&CK,
# RFCs, tool man pages) and organised BY ARTIFACT rather than by slide order.
# Propagate into `crates/data/src/catalog/descriptors/` — never publish the raw
# distillation. Descriptors cite the primary source, never the course.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SANS FOR508 / GCFA
research/gcfa-spine/
research/gcfa-knowledge-inventory.md

# 13cubed "Investigating Windows Endpoints" (paid course)
research/iwe-knowledge-inventory.md
research/iwe-forensicnomicon-reconciliation.md

# NOT ignored, deliberately: research/ingestion-corpus.md is our own TDD
# application log. Its course mentions are review notes ENFORCING this rule
# ("no blog/13cubed/SANS used as authority"), not distilled course content.

# Unanchored: cargo puts a `target/` under every package root, not only the repo
# root — `bindings/python/` and `fuzz/` each have one. A leading-slash pattern
# matches the repo root only, which is how build artifacts got committed.
target/
/data/
.DS_Store
.playwright-mcp/
# Ignore .claude/ CONTENTS (not the dir itself) so git still descends and the
# negation below can re-include the one deliberately-committed command file.
# Otherwise it is "tracked AND ignored", which trips cargo/release-plz's clean-tree check.
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/
.claude/commands/*
!.claude/commands/review-dfir-feeds.md
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
site/
